<h1>Robert &quot;Bob&quot; Rita</h1>
<p>Illinois House, 28th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Incumbent.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Has not published a platform for this race that we could find. Wikipedia lists his stated priorities as economic redevelopment, equitable school funding and increased health care availability; on ilga.gov he is Deputy Majority Leader and chairs the General Services appropriations committee.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>An operating engineer and member of IUOE Local 150 who has served in the House since 2003 and is also a Calumet Township Democratic committeeman and township trustee.</p>
